    <p class="prose">
      The distribution is <strong>significantly right-skewed</strong>, with a mean ($39.44) materially above the median ($29.10). The interquartile range of $43.11 spans the bulk of "normal" operating range from $17.50 to $60.61. Prices above $85.54 (the 90th percentile) represent genuinely extreme regimes—all concentrated in the 2008 supercycle peak and the 2011–2014 plateau. The coefficient of variation of 74.2% is exceptionally high for a commodity, reflecting the political and structural determinants of oil supply that are absent in agricultural or industrial commodities.
    </p>
    <p class="prose">
      The bimodal shape visible in the histogram—with clusters in the $10–30 range (1970s–1990s) and the $60–120 range (2000s–2020s)—is not statistical noise. It reflects a genuine structural shift in the global supply-demand equilibrium that took hold after 2003.
    </p>
